  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering the NES Palette**\n\nI\'m now contemplating overriding `Theme.kt` with a custom retro NES style! I\'m leaning toward a high-contrast dark palette, drawing inspiration from the original Legend of Zelda. Black will be the background, with prominent green, red, gold/orange, and white colors.\n\n\n**Implementing Pixel Art**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to implementing pixel art! My new idea involves generating retro-style visuals directly in Jetpack Compose, perfectly rendering NES sprites. I\'m thinking of using Kotlin pixel-art drawing functions, perhaps with `Canvas` or custom grids. We can represent sprites as arrays of strings or coordinates and draw them into pixel-perfect canvases. That would ensure crisp pixel grids. I need to review the database requirements first.\n\n\n**Analyzing Database Schema**\n\nI\'m now diving into the database schema! I\'m reviewing the custom Room entities for `Habit`, `SufferingItem`, and `DailyRun`. My main focus is on the data types and their suitability. I\'m exploring the best way to represent lists of habit IDs and how to handle dates effectively with Room, confirming that using `List` is supported.\n\n\n**Refining Database Design**\n\nI\'m now refining the database design, as I\'ve confirmed Moshi is already in the dependencies. I plan to serialize habit lists using JSON via Moshi to store the completed habit IDs, conquering suffering items, and user data. I am considering a `DailyRunEntity`, with the date as the primary key. I will probably also create a `ProfileEntity`, to store user XP and the current streak. I will likely calculate the current streak by counting consecutive `DailyRunEntity` instances.\n\n\n**Defining the Profile Schema**\n\nI\'ve decided on the `ProfileEntity` schema, including `xp`, `streak`, and `lastActiveDate`, with `id = 1` as the primary key. This approach is very straightforward, which is what I wanted. I\'ve been working on a robust data structure for the profile table.\n\n**Evaluating Initialization Requirements**\n\nI\'m now reading `strings.xml` and `metadata.json` to ensure the app name is initialized, as per guidelines. I\'ve noted that the metadata name is currently empty. I\'ve recognized that I *must* set a descriptive name in both files during this first turn and am considering \"Suffering Tracker.\"\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will read `strings.xml` to keep resource names synchronized and prepare to update the application name."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 254558347
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
