    thinking: "**Considering Sprite Configurations**\n\nOkay, I\'m now focusing on pixel art sprite configurations. I\'m aiming for beautiful, retro 8-bit drawings. I\'m planning to create a `ZeldaSprites.kt` file within the `com.example.ui` package to store these retro art patterns. I\'m envisioning various drawing utilities to accompany these configurations for pixel art drawing.\n\n\n**Designing Pixel Sprite Elements**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in designing a `PixelSprite` composable! My priority is to populate `ZeldaSprites.kt` with pixel art for a hero, heart, potions, shield, sword, chest, and a book. I\'m focusing on defining each graphic, followed by implementing a helper that can perfectly render any 2D string grid.\n\n\n**Defining Sprite Character Maps**\n\nI\'ve decided to create a character map for the sprite patterns, mapping characters to specific NES colors. I\'m assigning letters like \'K\' for black, \'W\' for white, \'R\' for red, etc., to streamline pattern definitions. This will also make the art creation much more legible! I\'m now developing the hero sprite, defining its 2D grid representation with these new character codes.\n\n\n**Refining Sprite Art**\n\nI\'ve revised the hero sprite to align perfectly with Link\'s iconic appearance, ensuring it\'s instantly recognizable and cute! I\'ve broken it down by hat, hair/face, tunic, and legs for clarity and easier modification. I\'ve also added the heart sprite.\n\n\n"
