  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Dialog Implementation**\n\nI\'m currently considering how to add dialog opening support for TavernPanel and ClosetPanel from MainLayout. TavernPanel currently defines its own state for dialog visibility. ClosetPanel, on the other hand, uses an on-screen form. I\'m exploring the implications of passing dialog state or a central dialog management system.\n\n\n**Designing Dialog Implementations**\n\nI\'m now designing how the gamepad will initiate dialogs within both TavernPanel and ClosetPanel. Button B will open different dialogs based on the active tab: a general habit dialog for the Tavern and a retro-styled AddWorryDialog for the Closet. I\'m leaning toward rendering these dialogs directly within MainLayout, potentially lifting state or using a central dialog management.\n\n\n**Refining Dialog Interactions**\n\nI\'m now refining the `AddWorryDialog` functionality. I\'m focusing on the `MainLayout` now, and how to enable us to submit anxiety and choose S, M, L size options from there! This is so much cleaner and interactive than the on-screen form, while still keeping that form available. I\'ve drafted an `AddWorryDialog` composable, complete with retro styling.\n\n\n**Implementing Worry Entry UI**\n\nI\'m now implementing the UI for entering worry details. I\'ve integrated an `OutlinedTextField` for the worry\'s name, styled with a retro aesthetic. I\'m focusing on the size selection UI, with options for small, medium, and large worries. I\'ve designed the UI with the NES styling guide in mind. It\'s looking good so far.\n\n\n**Finalizing Worry Input Details**\n\nI\'ve finalized the worry entry dialog\'s UI, incorporating size selection buttons with \'S\', \'M\', \'L\' labels. I added an abort button and a dump button. I\'m focusing on the dialog\'s dismiss and confirm actions. I\'m satisfied, I think it\'s ready.\n\n\n**Expanding Interaction Possibilities**\n\nI\'m now expanding the interaction options available to the user. I\'ve realized that the B button can open different dialogs depending on the location: a habit dialog in the Tavern, a worry dialog in the Closet, and a Sage instruction prompt in the Morgue. This is useful! Now, the start button will open a new \"SAGES\' START MENU\" dialog. It will include stats, instructions, and restart options. I\'ve begun composing this menu, and it looks beautiful.\n\n\n**Composing Start Menu**\n\nI\'m currently composing the \"SAGES\' START SCROLL\" dialog, starting with a title and a container for content. I\'m leveraging `Box` and `Column` for structure and spacing. The scroll will display status information with retro styling. It\'s looking to be a great, organized panel.\n\n\n**Displaying Stat Information**\n\nI\'m now integrating stats into the \"SAGES\' START SCROLL\" dialog. I\'ve successfully incorporated quest progress, total wisdom XP, and daily consecutive runs into the menu. I\'m using monospace font and retro styling to fit the NES aesthetic, using a dynamic font size. I think it looks very clean.\n\n\n**Adding Checkin Functionality**\n\nI\'m now adding a \"Replay Checkin\" button to the \"SAGES\' START SCROLL\" dialog, enabling users to repeat the checkin process. It will call a function `onManualCheckIn()` and close the menu. I\'m also implementing a close button with a subtle visual differentiation, all styled retro. It looks good and is coming together.\n\n\n**Adding Habit Toggle**\n\nI\'m now integrating the habit-checking functionality into the Button A handler within the `MainLayout`. I\'m using `todayRunState` to track completed habits and finding the first unchecked habit from `weightedHabits` to toggle. I will also be considering a Toast or dialog message for when all habits are checked.\n\n\n"
