  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the Implementation**\n\nI\'m now implementing the states for the dialogs, specifically `showAddWorryDialogFromMain` and `showAddHabitDialogFromMain` within `MainLayout`. These mutable states will control the visibility of the \"Add Worry\" and \"Add Habit\" dialogs from the main layout.\n\n\n**Integrating Dialogs into MainLayout**\n\nI\'m making progress integrating the dialogs within `MainLayout`. I\'ve verified the state management for controlling dialog visibility, focusing on `showAddWorryDialogFromMain`, `showAddHabitDialogFromMain`, and `showStartMenuDialog` . I can reuse the existing `AddHabitDialog` composable. Now, I\'m working to fully replace the existing `MainLayout` with the new component. I will ensure all elements from the design HTML are represented. I am also working on `completedIds`.\n\n\n**Implementing the Visuals**\n\nI\'m now focusing on implementing the visual design elements, specifically the theme styling and the \"MAP POS\" label. I plan to add the retro \"MAP POS: 7-G\" label below the `HeaderStatsBar` for that classic Zelda feel. I\'m also working on the \"Life Hearts\" representation for the streak, implementing the retro buttons and overall polished look. Finally, I\'m checking existing files to ensure full coverage during the rewrite. I\'m making sure to implement `HeaderStatsBar` with the new design.\n\n\n**Refining the Header Stats Bar**\n\nI am now actively working on refining the `HeaderStatsBar`. I\'m focusing on the \"Life\" representation, specifically the heart icons that visually indicate the user\'s streak. I\'m finalizing the logic for displaying the appropriate number of active and empty hearts based on the streak value. The goal is to accurately reflect a retro-style representation of life, with a minimum of one heart.\n\n\n**Visualizing the Inventory**\n\nI\'m now focused on visualizing the user\'s inventory and stats, particularly the display of experience points. I am working on displaying experience as \"X ###\", using the Diamond icon to represent experience, and incorporating monospace font and bold styling for the display.\n\n\n**Visualizing Inventory Items**\n\nI\'m now implementing the display of key and bomb items in the inventory. I\'ve integrated visual representations with the key and bomb icons, as well as the corresponding counts for active suffering and habits. The numbers are formatted as \"%02d\" for a consistent two-digit display. I\'m ensuring the counts are displayed with the proper monospace font, bold styling, and NES_WHITE color for a retro aesthetic.\n\n\n**Considering Component Reuse**\n\nI\'m now considering the reuse of `HeaderStatsBar`. I\'ve realized its also used inside of `TavernPanel`, and `ClosetPanel`, which could simplify the overall structure. I\'m assessing how I can integrate and maintain consistency across these diverse components.\n\n\n**Confirming Code Integration**\n\nI\'m now confirming the logic within `MainLayout`. I\'ve verified the code handles both `TAVERN` and `CLOSET` panel scenarios. I\'ve double-checked the logic and confirmed that the actions on button clicks within the panels behave correctly. The integration of state handlers and interactive buttons is proceeding as planned. I\'m satisfied that everything will compile and work as desired.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
