  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing a Character Creator**\n\nI\'m excited! I\'m moving forward with a character creator. My focus is on customizable sprites, specifically an NES style. I\'ve got two initial choices: Link Warrior (standard Link) and Sage Elder (cloaked magic). I am considering this carefully.\n\n\n**Exploring Character Options**\n\nI\'ve considered new character archetypes, adding a Zelda Princess/Mage and a Stalfos/Dark Hero to the potential roster. I\'m also exploring color customization for sprite parts: cap/cloak, accents, and skin tone. I\'ve now begun to figure out the user interface, and am deciding how to best implement the Character Creator inside the Tavern Board. I\'m considering new buttons, a card, or a persistent section.\n\n\n**Implementing the Creator Interface**\n\nI\'ve decided on the character creator UI; a dedicated \"+ CHARACTER CREATOR\" button is the best. I think placing it in the `TavernPanel` (or directly inside `HeaderStatsBar`!) is intuitive. I am looking at adding it near \"+ FORGE BUFF\" or in a Row to maintain consistency with other elements, like how I see lines 636-666 in my code.\n\n\n**Refining Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m solidifying the UI design. I\'m imagining two retro buttons in the `TavernPanel`. One is \"+ FORGE BUFF\", and the new is \"\360\237\233\241\357\270\217 CHARACTER\". The \"\360\237\233\241\357\270\217 CHARACTER\" button will trigger a full-screen dialogue with a live pixel art preview and options to choose from: Warrior, Sage, Paladin, or Fairy. They can select retro color themes or customize primary/secondary outfits and hair.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will search the codebase for usages of `ZeldaSprites` to see all the places where the pixel sprite is shown."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 855013866
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
