riables, making sprite patterns like HERO (Link) incredibly flexible. My focus is now on the SAGE pattern\'s design, using the same grid style for easy recoloring with the palette mapping.\n\n\n**Designing Character Sprites**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing the Warrior (HERO) and Sage (SAGE) sprites, using a character-based matrix for customizability. I\'m focusing on the characters such as `W`, `D`, `G`, `Y`, `P`, and `B` for Warrior. For the Sage, I plan to design using characters for the robes, hood, and beard, aiming for a distinctive appearance.\n\n\n**Defining Fairy (FAIRY)**\n\nI\'m now focusing on designing a fairy sprite using a matrix, similar to the previous characters. I\'m assigning color variables like `Y` for the pixie, `G` for wings, `K` for a dark body and wings shadow, `W` for a light pixie glow and `P` for the sparkles, to define this pattern.\n\n\n"
