  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully fixed the `IllegalStateException` preventing the app from launching.\n\n### \360\237\224\215 Cause of the Bug\nThe database error occurred because `insertProfile` inside `AppRepository.kt` wrapped the database call using the synchronous, blocking transaction method `db.runInTransaction` on Room. Because the initialization routine in `MainViewModel` resides in `viewModelScope.launch` which defaults to the UI main dispatcher, attempting to invoke a blocking transaction on the main thread triggered Room\'s safety check and generated the crash.\n\n### \360\237\233\240\357\270\217 Solution Implemented\n* **Repository Isolation & Async Integrity**: Modified `/app/src/main/java/com/example/data/Repository.kt` to call the native suspending DAO input function `profileDao.insertProfile(profile)` directly without wrapping it in a blocking `db.runInTransaction`. Room\'s suspending interfaces handle thread pools (`Dispatchers.IO`) under the hood safely and automatically.\n* **Compilation & Test Suite Verification**:\n  * Ran `compile_applet` which successfully concluded with zero errors.\n  * Ran full unit test routines with passing coverage."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
