  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Examining the Database**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the database schema, specifically `Entities.kt`. I\'m looking closely at the `DailyRunEntity` and considering how it relates to habit tracking. The use of a CSV for storing completed habit IDs looks interesting from a data persistence perspective.\n\n\n**Refining Habit Tracking**\n\nI\'m now diving into the `toggleHabit` function within `MainViewModel.kt` to understand how habit completion is currently managed. It seems the function already handles adding and removing habit IDs to the `completedHabitIdsCsv` based on whether the habit is checked or unchecked. My goal is to determine if this implementation can be easily adapted to record the order of completion. I think I will need to capture the exact order.\n\n\n**Confirming Habit Order**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that appending habit IDs to `completedHabitIdsCsv` inherently captures completion order, which is great news! My next thought focuses on presenting this execution order within the daily summary. It\'s becoming clear that this order information can enhance the daily report. Additionally, I\'m thinking about the user\'s daily self-reported mood, which is captured when a new day begins, and I\'m currently looking for the logic that determines a \"new day\".\n\n\n**Investigating Check-in Flow**\n\nI\'ve traced the logic for displaying the morning check-in questionnaire. The absence of a run for the current day, indicated by `latestRun` not matching `todayDateStr`, triggers the check-in. This leads me to want to examine `MainLayout.kt` to understand how the questionnaire is rendered. I am now looking at the file itself, and I am curious how large it is.\n\n\n"
