    thinking: "**Capturing Daily Mood**\n\nI\'ve got it! The user\'s mood, as self-reported for the completed day, needs to be the initial value every time the app opens. I\'ll need to make sure the game logic relies on that reported mood to start the next day\'s run.\n\n\n**Summarizing Yesterday\'s Progress**\n\nNow I\'m thinking about what comes *after* the mood is entered. I need to display a summary of the *previous* day: completed habits in order, the reported mood, and a trend graph of previous moods. Tapping the most recent entry should allow modifying habit completion data. I also need to make sure that the system provides the ability to add, remove, and move around habits in the daily record, as well as add general notes about the day.\n\n\n**Clarifying Display Sequence**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the best way to present the previous day\'s summary. Should it be a distinct screen, a panel within the check-in view, or an overlay? Perhaps it appears after mood selection, with a clear \"START NEW DAY\" button. I\'m also considering how to best handle habit modification within the summary.\n\n\n**Refining Check-In Flow**\n\nI\'m solidifying the transition from mood check-in to a daily summary. The idea is to present a \"Daily Summary Screen\" after mood input, which will display completed habits, the reported mood, and a mood trend graph. I\'m focusing on how the UI allows modification of habit completion, noting it has to happen somewhere the user will be able to get to it in an intuitive manner.\n\n\n"
