  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Verifying Data Changes**\n\nI\'ve confirmed that `fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` is active with Room version `2`. This enables a safe version increment to `3`, and adding `notableEvents` to `DailyRunEntity`. Now, I\'m verifying all related files for required modifications. Specifically, I\'m examining `DailyRunEntity` itself for related adjustments.\n\n\n**Analyzing Design Requirements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on integrating the design requirements into the `DailyRunEntity`. The \"notable events\" field seems key here. I\'m considering how this field, along with the other data, supports mood capture, habit management, and the addition of \"notable events\". I\'m also ensuring the data structure accommodates chronological habit completion order and mood trends.\n\n\n**Reviewing Check-in Tracking**\n\nI\'m now examining the check-in tracking mechanism. I\'ve pinpointed `MainViewModel`, specifically the `_showCheckIn` and `_checkInDate` `StateFlow` variables, and their role in displaying the morning check-in questionnaire. I\'m also reviewing `submitCheckInMood` to understand how mood data is integrated into existing run data, and updating the profile streak.\n\n\n**Refining Check-In Workflow**\n\nI\'m now contemplating how to refine the check-in process. Specifically, I\'m considering the transition from mood selection to a summary view. I\'ve narrowed down potential approaches: introducing a `_showSummary` state, or incorporating sub-phases within the check-in panel. The latter could allow viewing previous data and trends alongside the entered mood. This seems like it should have a more consistent flow for the user.\n\n\n**Designing Interactive Editor**\n\nI\'m now building out an interactive editor for completed habits on the daily summary page, and ensuring that this can be used on the most recent day. I\'m focusing on the functionality to add, remove, and move habits to reflect their completion order. I\'ll also add an option to include general \"notable events\" for context, along with a recent display of previous day\'s moods to show trends. I\'m also ensuring this interactive editor can be reached from the Morning Check-In Summary flow and the `MorguePanel`.\n\n\n**Defining Habit Ordering**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the interactive editor\'s design. The plan involves updating `DailyRunEntity` directly. The key is allowing modification of both `completedHabitIdsCsv` and `notableEvents`. I\'m also considering a two-phase check-in: mood entry, followed by a summary view. This summary will offer an editor to refine habit execution order by adding, removing, and moving habits. This all follows the logic defined.\n\n\n**Refining Editor Interaction**\n\nI\'m now refining the habit editor\'s interaction. Instead of complex position controls, I\'m leaning toward a list displaying the current execution order, with \"+\" buttons between habits for insertion points. This gives an elegant, intuitive UI. There will also be a \"Notable Events\" text input, which is saved in `notableEvents`. I\'m also planning to show the previous 7 days\' mood trends, and a \"BEGIN TODAY\'S ADVENTURE\" button to start the day. I\'m also wondering if edits should be possible for the most recent run from the Morgue.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view the `MorguePanel` implementation in `MainLayout.kt` to see how past runs are currently visualised and styled."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 17202238
    }
