  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Display Functionality**\n\nI\'m focusing now on displaying the feature effectively. I need to design the user experience thoughtfully and robustly. I\'m currently looking at how habits are managed and their order. They seem to be stored as comma-separated IDs in `completedHabitIdsCsv`. This will inform how I approach displaying the execution order.\n\n\n**Refining Data Display**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data presentation, specifically the run habit order. I\'m thinking the app should capture the previous day\'s mood upon opening, showcasing a summary with habit order and recent mood trends. I\'m working out details about user interaction within recent days, including editing habits, adding new ones between existing entries, and including general events. I\'m focusing on incorporating a new flow into the `MainViewModel` for updating CSVs and notable events.\n\n\n**Structuring Check-In Process**\n\nI\'m now reorganizing the check-in process logic. I\'m focusing on the `MorningCheckInState` with two states: `SELECT_MOOD` and `SHOW_SUMMARY`. `SELECT_MOOD` prompts for the previous day\'s mood. Then, I can show a `SHOW_SUMMARY` panel, displaying the chosen mood, an execution order checklist (or a message if none completed), and an editable section for habit adjustments. This new structure streamlines the user flow.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Editing**\n\nI\'m now integrating an interactive habit order manager directly into the summary view for effortless user control. I\'m prioritizing direct interaction. I\'ve added a button to expand an editable list of completed habits, with \"Move Up,\" \"Move Down,\" and \"Remove\" options per habit. Below, I\'m incorporating a control to add habits from a list of incomplete ones, with placement options. This lets users insert habits as needed, and next I\'ll be working on integrating a text input for notable event entry.\n\n\n**Refining User Experience**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on UI details. I\'m adding a retro text field for notable events, with dynamic saving on edit for responsiveness. Also, I\'m working on a display of the past seven days\' moods, dates, and progress, revealing recent trends. I\'m focusing on user flow optimization, and adding a clear \"PROCEED TO NEW RUN\" button to conclude the check-in process. I\'m aiming for seamless interaction. Finally, I\'m double-checking the editability of previous runs for a robust user experience.\n\n\n**Expanding Editing Access**\n\nI\'m now expanding the accessibility of the editing tools. I realized the summary panel is the natural spot to directly manage the most recent day. I\'m also adding a button in the `MorguePanel` (Sages\' Morgue) on each historic log entry to \"\360\237\223\235 CUSTOMIZE HABITS & EVENTS FOR THIS RUN\", enabling direct editing from the logs. This will fulfill all the requirements.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `MainActivity.kt` to see how the app starts up and how ViewModel is constructed."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 583818385
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
