  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Designing Check-In UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on designing the custom UI panels for check-in. The core features I\'m working to support are mood entry for completed days and displaying a comprehensive summary. This summary will include the order of habit completion, mood, and a trend display of previous days\' moods.\n\n\n**Enhancing Check-In Interaction**\n\nI\'m now thinking about interactive editing within the check-in summary. I envision users adding, removing, and moving habits freely, even inserting them \"between\" existing ones. \"Notable Events\" will be recordable too. There will be a button to end the summary review, starting the new day. Looking at `MorningCheckInPanel` in `MainLayout.kt`, I realized a two-phase check-in process would be better than an immediate submission.\n\n\n**Simplifying View Model Logic**\n\nI\'m now reconsidering the role of `MainViewModel`. By handling the check-in process entirely within `MorningCheckInPanel`, I can keep the view model very lightweight. The key is passing the necessary data from `MainLayout` to `MorningCheckInPanel`, such as the list of habits. I\'m moving toward a design where the check-in interaction is self-contained within the panel itself, which avoids unnecessary complexity. The state management can be handled locally now.\n\n\n**Reviewing Data Accessibility**\n\nI\'m now focusing on how `MorningCheckInPanel` will access necessary information. It\'s becoming clearer that passing the `MainViewModel` directly will simplify things. I\'ll include the `checkInDate` and a `heroSprite` as parameters to `MorningCheckInPanel`. Investigating the `submitCheckInMood` function in the `MainViewModel` has revealed the data handling.\n\n\n**Revising Check-In Logic**\n\nI\'m now changing my strategy for the check-in process! I realized that I can dynamically display a summary of a *past* run, by updating the run when `onSubmitMood` is called, and transition our local step to \"show summary\"! This requires an update to the current step within `MorningCheckInPanel`, but avoids immediately closing the check-in. The local state management is key to providing this.\n\n\n**Refining Check-In Workflow**\n\nI\'m now implementing the ability for users to edit a past run directly before starting a new day. A new state variable will track the check-in step. I\'m thinking of creating a `registerCheckInMood(mood: Int)` to update the mood and keep the check-in panel open. This requires changes in the `MainViewModel`, specifically to `submitCheckInMood`. The logic will award XP and update the database, but it won\'t automatically close the dialog. A new function, perhaps `completeCheckIn()`, will handle finalization.\n\n\n**Implementing Data Persistence**\n\nI\'ve just added database updates for both successful past run updates and the handling of potentially missing run entities. The flow also updates the user\'s profile streak and awards XP based on the check-in data. This covers the critical database interactions for modifying mood, streak calculations, and XP awards when a run is edited.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view lines 101 to 140 of `MainViewModel.kt` to see how morning check-in state is processed and saved in the database."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 207155568
    }
