l, Hero?\" I\'ve made the text centered, using monospace, and styled it with `NES_WHITE`. I\'m using a spacer to add some height before and after the text for visual clarity. Finally, I\'ve added a mood selection block to get user feedback.\n\n\n**Expanding The Editing**\n\nI\'m expanding the editable runs concept! Instead of simple read-only breakdowns, `MorguePanel` will support editing *any* past run using a new `RunSummaryEditorPanel`! This would allow users to add, remove, and move habits within a run log. I can also integrate the option to add notable events for any day, enhancing the logging experience. This is elegant and robust!\n\n\n**Implementing The Button**\n\nNow, I\'m integrating an \"Edit Adventure Log\" button within the expanded state of a historic run in `MorguePanel`!  I\'m exploring two approaches: either show a read-only view with the button, or directly display the `RunSummaryEditorPanel` as a dialog or expanded card. The key is to pass the required state, `viewModel`, `allHabits`, and `runs`, to the `HistoricRunRowItem` function for proper handling. I\'m focusing on modifying the `HistoricRunRowItem` signature to accept and use this new state.\n\n\n**Designing The Interface**\n\nI\'ve got it! Modifying `HistoricRunRowItem` allows a beautiful solution. Clicking \"EDIT ADVENTURE LOG\" toggles a dialog containing the `RunSummaryEditorPanel`. This provides a clean, fullscreen editor with a \"CLOSE & SAVE LOG\" action! I\'ve visualized the flow: expand row, click button, edit in dialog, and close/save. The custom dialog delivers a professional UX for any daily run!\n\n\n**Unifying The Experience**\n\nI\'m now integrating a \"CUSTOMIZE HABITS & NOTABLE EVENTS\" button into the workflow. Clicking it will launch a dialog. Inside, the `RunSummaryEditorPanel` will show, the same one for daily check-ins! This unified approach is fantastic, providing a consistent user experience for editing past runs and the daily log. This streamlines the code, and delivers a robust UX.\n\n\n**Reviewing The Parameters**\n\nI\'m now confirming the parameters needed by `HistoricRunRowItem`. It looks like I don\'t need any changes, as `MorguePanel` already has the necessary `viewModel`, `runs`, and `habits`. I\'m confirming that all the palette elements are already available. The existing setup works, so I\'m moving forward with a call to add those. I\'m now ready to call `HistoricRunRowItem`!\n\n\n"
