    modified_response: "I have successfully implemented the requested features for managing habit completion order, notable events, and mood reviews in **Hero\'s Habit Run**:\n\n### Key Advancements\n\n1. **Chronological Habit Execution Order**:\n   - Modified `DailyRunEntity` with a new `notableEvents` text field to support logging the external factors influencing the character\'s status.\n   - Refactored `MorningCheckInPanel` into a multi-phase check-in flow:\n     - **Phase 1: Mood check-in**: Prompts the user with a retro selection card for great, meh, or hard runs.\n     - **Phase 2: Adventure Log**: Opens an interactive `RunSummaryEditorPanel` visualizing the completed habits (buffs) in their exact execution order, showing trends of past days, and exposing interactive customization features.\n\n2. **Unified Execution Editor (`RunSummaryEditorPanel`)**:\n   - Fully interactive controls for managing completion checklists without leaving the screen.\n   - **Adding/Inserting Buffs**: Prompts the user to pick any habit and choose its placement location\342\200\224whether at the beginning, at the end, or *directly between previously logged ones* (e.g., \"After Step #2\").\n   - **Reordering & Removal**: Exposes intuitive `\342\226\262` (Move Up), `\342\226\274` (Move Down), and `\342\235\214` (Remove) action icons per logged step to custom tweak completion logs.\n   - **Memorable Factors Editor**: Features a beautiful dark retro input text area to type out any sleep patterns, weather factors, or notable occurrences contributing to daily mood states.\n   - **Integrated Trends**: Shows a 7-day mood graph right above the confirmation step to track current progressions.\n\n3. **Past Run Customization**:\n   - Upgraded `HistoricRunRowItem` in the Sages\' Morgue (`MorguePanel`) to accept `viewModel` actions.\n   - Users can now click into **any historic logging day** (including the most recent ones), read the logs, and click a clean retro button to open the `RunSummaryEditorPanel` in a dedicated dialog. Any past chronological sequencing or memos can be fine-tuned securely.\n"
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
